          "answer": "To add a new character to your story bible, I need two things from you:\n\n1.  **The Character's Name**: This is required to identify them.\n2.  **A Description**: You can provide this in any way that's easiest for you—a rough paragraph, a list of traits, or even just a messy brain-dump of notes.\n\n**How I handle it:**\nI will take your description and map it to the specific \"Character\" details used in your world (such as their physical appearance, personality, background, or motivations). \n\n**The Process:**\n*   **You provide the info:** Just tell me about the character.\n*   **I propose the entry:** I won't just add it silently. I will create a \"draft\" entry in your review inbox.\n*   **You approve:** You'll see a card with the structured details I've extracted. Once you click **Apply**, they are officially part of your story bible.\n\n**Pro-tip:** If you have a whole list of characters or a chapter where new people are introduced, you can just paste the whole text, and I'll extract them all at once for your review."
